history_panel = f'<div class="panel"><h3>Keep archive writes off the editing path.</h3><p>A deterministic {history_bench["rows"]:,}-transcript archive ({history_bench["archive_bytes"]/1e6:.2f} MB) and {history_bench["edits"]} rapid edits measured <strong>{old_history["edit_p50_ms"]:.2f} ms → {new_history["edit_p50_ms"]:.2f} ms p50</strong> for mutation, retention filtering and persistence admission. The serial background writer made {new_history["writes"]} write instead of {old_history["writes"]}; its final flush took {new_history["flush_ms"]:.0f} ms. Final files were byte-identical.</p><p class="small muted">Synthetic storage-path benchmark, fixed legacy-first order, no filesystem/thermal isolation. It does not measure SwiftUI frames or human typing cadence. Edits coalesce for 300 ms and flush on orderly quit; an abrupt crash can lose an unflushed edit. New recordings keep recovery audio until saved history is confirmed. Launch loading and search indexing remain work. <a href="../benchmarks/results/history-persistence.json">Raw receipt and source/executable fingerprints</a>.</p></div>'
