page = page.replace("</section>\n<section id=\"models\">", '<details><summary>Native Deepgram BYOK: a separate prerecorded API.</summary><p>OSpr sends locally normalized audio to Listen using Token authentication. The Nova-3 preset supports vocabulary phrases, explicit or detected language, and utterance/word timing. Automatic number formatting stays off; fillers are requested. Cloud speaker labels and summaries are not requested. Independent parts retain full timeline offsets and repeated text, with no completed partial transcript after failure or cancellation.</p><p>The contract tests caught and fixed literal-plus encoding for C++. Malformed timing keeps the text with coarse boundaries. An 80-minute public fixture passed every-sample binary transport and word/utterance offset checks through the real Swift CLI and worker against a loopback server. This is not cloud recognition, paid-account validation, a speed benchmark or live streaming. Native provider selection, Keychain restart, 80-minute binary import and persisted text/word/utterance offsets passed. The fixture server was stopped after the test; live preference restoration is tracked separately in the native acceptance receipt.</p><p class="small muted">Blank language requests provider detection, which may select another supported model. <a href="https://developers.deepgram.com/reference/speech-to-text/listen-pre-recorded">API reference</a> · <a href="https://developers.deepgram.com/docs/keyterm">Keyterms</a> · <a href="https://developers.deepgram.com/docs/language-detection">Detection policy</a> · <a href="data/deepgram-contract.json">Checked contract</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/deepgram-upload-parts.json">Raw transport receipt</a>.</p></details>' + "</section>\n<section id=\"models\">")
