    product_panel = '<details><summary>Actual product CLIs: the original startup gap.</summary><p>The official signed and notarized Vibe 3.2.2 desktop CLI forwards to its bundled server. It was compared with OSpr’s bundled CLI on 20 preselected speakers: the first utterance from the first ten speakers in each existing clean/other manifest. Three fresh processes per case and configuration produced 180 commands in seeded random order. Quality uses repeat zero only, totaling 485 reference words; timings use all trials.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Product / model route</th><th>Cases / trials</th><th>First-repeat WER</th><th>Fresh command p50</th><th>Fresh command p95</th><th>Failed commands</th></tr></thead><tbody>' + ''.join(rows) + '</tbody></table></div><p>Vibe completed these fresh commands sooner. This identifies a startup gap. A separate instrumented worker boot attributed about 901 ms inclusive to scipy.signal imports during 1,121 ms of boot; cumulative module times overlap and instrumentation perturbs timings. The instrumented diagnostic alone does not establish an execution-path improvement; see the repeated candidate pilot below. The quality totals differ by only one or two word errors, which does not establish an accuracy winner.</p><p class="small muted">Fresh model contexts with already primed OS file/shader caches. Default language and trimming behavior differ, as do the Turbo conversions/runtimes. Vibe used Metal on M5 Max, with its optional tensor API unavailable; analytics were disabled. Shared desktop activity and no thermal or energy isolation. These are file-command results, separate from the warm decoder plot. They exclude GUI, microphone, hotkey, endpointing, rewriting and insertion, and do not establish a top-three product ranking. <a href="../benchmarks/results/product-cli.json">All 180 trials and exact settings</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/startup-imports-parakeet-v3.json">Import diagnostic</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/vibe-release-provenance.json">Official-release, signature, version and GPU provenance</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/README.md">Reproduction</a>.</p></details>'
