    startup_panel = '<details open id="startup-candidate"><summary>Startup optimization: repeated product-command pilot.</summary><p>The identical frozen pilot was rerun on the signed candidate bundle: the same 20 public speakers, three fresh processes per route and seeded serial order. Vibe is rerun as a control. OSpr now imports SciPy resampling only when needed and loads the fixed Parakeet mel bank from verified numerical data. Model construction/evaluation, strict weights and precision remain the upstream path.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Product / route</th><th>Before p50</th><th>Candidate p50</th><th>Candidate p95</th><th>Before → candidate WER</th><th>Candidate failures / trials</th></tr></thead><tbody>' + ''.join(rows) + '</tbody></table></div><p>All 697 parameter arrays (627,052,166 values), preprocessing values and mel filters matched upstream exactly. All 515 public-suite texts, segments and word timings also matched; all normalized inputs and eight sample-rate controls stayed bit-identical. This equivalence check is separate from the timing pilot.</p><p class="small muted">The product pilot uses 16 kHz read-speech files and already primed OS caches. A first native-rate input still needs resampling; explicit model preparation now primes that path at 48 kHz. Shared desktop activity prevents attributing every before/after timing difference solely to code. These command timings exclude microphone, GUI, endpointing, rewriting and insertion. Tiny WER gaps do not establish an accuracy winner or top-three ranking. <a href="../benchmarks/results/product-cli-after-startup.json">All candidate trials</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/product-cli.json">Original trials</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/startup-imports-after.json">Candidate import diagnostic</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/parakeet-loader-equivalence.json">Parameter and decoded-output equivalence</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/audio-input-equivalence.json">Normalization controls</a>.</p></details>'
