    migration = history_index["migration"]
    history_panel = f'<details id="indexed-history"><summary>Large-history storage prototype: {history_index["rows"]:,} timing-rich records.</summary><p>The previous JSON history decoded the whole archive at startup and scanned every row for search. Current source connects a SQLite engine to summary pages, aggregate counts and a selected detail on demand; generated-fixture native history acceptance has passed. The synthetic fixture has {history_index["fixture"]["bytes"]/1e6:.1f} MB of legacy JSON. Three fresh child processes per route keep full JSON decoding out of the indexed process’s peak-memory measurement.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Storage route</th><th>Initial data p50</th><th>Observed p95</th><th>Process peak RSS p50</th></tr></thead><tbody>' + ''.join(history_rows) + '</tbody></table></div><p>Initial data means counts, the first 100 list rows and one complete selected transcript. Both routes returned equal counts, all top-100 IDs for eight literal queries, and the same selected-record payload hash. Migration separately checks an ordered digest of every full source payload against persisted data before committing and removing the verified legacy file.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Literal query</th><th>JSON scan p50</th><th>Indexed route p50</th></tr></thead><tbody>' + ''.join(search_rows) + f'</tbody></table></div><p>One-time migration plus initial data took {migration["initial_data_ms"]/1000:.2f} s, with {migration["peak_rss_bytes"]/1024**2:.1f} MiB peak RSS. The resulting database occupies {migration["database_bytes"]/1e6:.1f} MB; indexing and row layout have a disk cost. An earlier migration exposed retained FileHandle read buffers; per-read autorelease pools now bound those temporaries. The earlier measured migration receipt is retained for comparison. A rejected 8 KiB page control saved only 0.3% disk space and raised the observed migration peak; the default remains 4 KiB.</p><p class="small muted">Prototype storage measurements on one shared Mac, with primed OS caches and synthetic repeated text. Timings begin after CLI dispatch and exclude process spawn. Three trials do not establish a tail-latency SLA. These are not app launch, SwiftUI rendering or human search measurements. The serial async repository now has tested coalescing, failure retry, delete/clear barriers and canceled reads. Repository/settings wiring and the paged UI are now implemented with presentation/application regression tests. Native history acceptance passed on a separate 235-record fixture profile. Package verification is a separate gate; the earlier preview still uses JSON. Session-only core transitions now have failure and no-file-open regression tests. <a href="../benchmarks/results/history-index.json">Every current trial and exact provenance</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/history-migration-memory-before.json">Earlier migration memory</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/history-index-8192-pages.json">Rejected 8 KiB control</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/history-sqlite-compatibility.json">Five SQLite runtimes and forty-five controls</a> · <a href="architecture/indexed-history.md">Storage contract and integration gates</a> · <a href="https://www.sqlite.org/fts5.html">SQLite FTS5 reference</a>.</p></details>'
