    profile_panel = f'''<details id="context-profiles"><summary>Current source: app/site rules and per-take model, language and instructions.</summary><p>Profiles match exact bundle IDs and optional HTTP(S) origins with segment-bounded path prefixes. The longest matching site path wins before app/global fallback. An immutable snapshot chooses mode, local model, recognition-language hint, Custom instruction and translation target when dictation starts. Global settings choose provider routes, credentials, insertion and retention. Imports and desktop recordings use their existing explicit settings.</p><p>URL lookup runs only for an enabled site rule in the captured app. It follows at most 24 same-process ancestors and reads the outer web-area/window URL metadata, without reading page text, address-bar values or clipboard content. Observed query/fragment is stripped and no captured URL enters settings/history/provider payload. Temporary per-object timeouts are restored before insertion. An 80 ms admission deadline is a query policy, not a measured latency SLA. Focused-object ownership is checked before selected-text capture and insertion.</p><p>The editor adds app selection, enable/disable, naming, editing and duplicate-rule validation. Studio shows the active model/style and the HUD identifies the profile. Legacy app-only settings decode; modern rules encode inactive for older decoders so site conditions cannot broaden to a whole app. Local source {esc(profiles["build"]["git_commit"][:7])} passes {profiles["checks"]["swift_tests"]} Swift / {profiles["checks"]["python_tests"]} Python tests, release build and lint. Twenty new Swift contracts and 17 real CLI dry-run cases cover boundaries, snapshots, compatibility, validation and privacy.</p><p class="small muted">Native startup and Modes presentation passed in an isolated profile. On Add profile, the automation service crashed during inspection; OSpr remained alive. Normal OSpr was restored with unchanged settings/history and no QA recording. Sheet visual/save/restart, actual Chrome/Safari URL discovery, live model/language switching and insertion remain open. The context-profiles-v0 preview below includes this source; earlier previews are preserved. <a href="architecture/context-profiles.md">Design, compatibility and reproduction</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/context-profiles-validation.json">Validation</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/context-profile-cli.json">CLI cases</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/context-profiles-native-ui.json">Native boundary</a> · <a href="data/context-profiles-contract.json">Primary references</a>.</p></details>'''
