    vad_panel = f'''<details id="neural-vad"><summary>Research: neural speech detection, quiet-input losses and endpoint tradeoffs.</summary><p>Frozen source {esc(vad["git_commit"][:7])} replays 179 public development cases: forty speakers with original, −40 dB gain and nominal 10 dB Gaussian-noise variants, five synthetic negatives, four AMI prefixes and fifty multilingual clips. Hardware: {esc(checked["hardware"]["chip"])}, {checked["hardware"]["memory_bytes"]/1024**3:g} GiB RAM, macOS {esc(checked["hardware"]["macos"])}. All {checked["swift_tests"]} Swift/{checked["python_tests"]} Python tests pass. A native WAV short-read control exposed 533 unread frames; the new bounded reader now drains the declared timeline.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Detector</th><th>Input hop</th><th>Prediction p95</th><th>Empty −40 dB edges</th><th>Negatives arming</th><th>AMI timing-proxy F1</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(rows)}</tbody></table></div><p>The AMI proxy marks 70.6% of frames as speech; an always-speech predictor would score F1 0.828 while arming on every negative and never finding silence. F1 alone cannot select a writing-tool gate. The primary 32 ms candidate improves observed Parakeet edge-trim WER, but two attenuated utterances still become empty. It is not promoted to an app default. Endpoint cuts are a distinct experiment: a 1.2 s silence rule can stop inside a read utterance and does not understand semantic completion.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Parakeet input</th><th>Original WER</th><th>−40 dB WER</th><th>Noise WER</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(quality_rows)}</tbody></table></div><p>There are 750 quality records, {checked["distinct_model_inferences"]} distinct actual model inferences, {vad["asr"]["unique_inferred_or_bypassed_inputs"]-checked["distinct_model_inferences"]} unique empty-input bypasses and reused equal inputs. The independent check verifies every input/model hash, replays 537 native event traces and recomputes score arithmetic. A follow-up causal eight-frame score removes the two empty edges on the stored development traces and retains all five negatives; its ASR and excluded-speaker checks are still open.</p><p class="small muted">At this frozen source the GUI and preview use RMS. Newer source integration is tracked in Progress. These are reused public development fixtures; electrical attenuation is not real whispering, synthetic noise is not a microphone route, and AMI word/segment masks are coarse proxies. Versions and 32/256 ms aggregation differ. Resident prediction timing excludes loading, priming, file I/O, resampling, queue scheduling and ASR; OS caches may be warm. Requested GPU/ANE/all eligibility is not proof of actual placement. No production false-stop, power or product-ranking claim. <a href="architecture/neural-endpointing.md">Contracts and integration gates</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/vad-candidate-v1.json">Result and ASR hypotheses</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/vad-candidate-v1.traces.json.gz">Every raw probability/time/event</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/vad-candidate-v1-validation.json">Independent checks</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/fixtures/vad-models.json">Pinned models</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/fixtures/vad-protocol.json">Preselected protocol</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/vad-causal8-development.json">Causal development derivation</a>.</p></details>'''
