    panel = f'''<details id="causal-vad-validation"><summary>Excluded-speaker validation: fewer quiet-input failures, model-dependent accuracy and longer finish delay.</summary><p>Frozen source {esc(causal["git_commit"][:7])} evaluates 33 speakers excluded from VAD development: 99 transformed speech cases and five reused synthetic negatives. All three local ASR models finish the eleven preselected input policies, yielding 3,432 quality records and {causal_checked["actual_asr_inferences"]:,} actual inferences. Independent checks verify {causal_checked["exact_causal_score_frames"]:,} exact causal scores, 312 native/reference event traces, every ASR input range/reuse flag and score arithmetic. Separate source-bound CI passes 263 Swift / 105 Python tests and 17 profile CLI cases.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>ASR / input</th><th>Original WER</th><th>−40 dB WER</th><th>Noise WER</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(rows)}</tbody></table></div><p>Causal edges and combined chains introduce zero new empty transcripts across 297 speech/model pairs. Unsmooth raw edges introduce one Parakeet empty; default RMS edges empty 30/33 attenuated inputs per model. Neural policies never arm the five negatives. Whisper hallucinates text on all five full/endpoint-only negatives; causal edges and chains bypass them all, while RMS edges still hallucinate on four.</p><p>Accuracy does not improve on every input. Relative to full audio, causal edges improve/equal/worsen 10/75/14 transformed Parakeet utterances, 8/84/7 Whisper utterances and 14/77/8 Cohere utterances. The receipts retain lexical regressions such as Captain Lake → Captain Leake. Written number formatting also counts in normalized WER. Edge and combined-chain bounds happen to match on this slice.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Policy</th><th>Original finish p95</th><th>−40 dB finish p95</th><th>Noise finish p95</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(delay_rows)}</tbody></table></div><p>All 99 speech cases finish after their source clip end; the causal maximum delay is 2.279 s. The 224 ms history span is not a bound on finish delay: continuing weak scores can sustain activity. The raw 1.424 s control does not match observed causal delays. Source clip end is a conservative content proxy, not last-phoneme timing or a live UI measurement. Default RMS finishes none of the noisy cases and prematurely finishes the three attenuated cases it arms.</p><p class="small muted">Decision: eligible for an explicit experimental integration, with defaults unchanged. Defaults and the delivered preview retain RMS; newer source integration is tracked separately. These speakers appeared in earlier ASR research; this is not a sealed ASR holdout. Transforms share source utterances, attenuation is not real whispering, the negatives are reused synthetic controls and RMS polling is approximated. No microphone, scheduling, power or product ranking acceptance. <a href="architecture/neural-endpointing.md">Contracts, tradeoffs and integration gates</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/fixtures/vad-causal8-validation-protocol.json">Frozen protocol</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/vad-causal8-validation.json">Every hypothesis and summary</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/vad-causal8-validation.traces.json.gz">Raw traces</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/vad-causal8-validation-checks.json">Independent checks</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/vad-causal8-ci.json">CI</a>.</p></details>'''
