    panel = f'''<details id="neural-auto-finish-ui"><summary>Neural auto finish milestone: verified model repair and native Settings Save.</summary><p>Source {esc(ui["build"]["git_commit"][:7])} exposes Neural auto finish · experimental in Settings, with a separately prepared local speech detector. The Models screen adds the {prepared["artifact_bytes"]/1e6:.2f} MB MIT asset. Microphone startup is cache-only and verifies all five pinned files again before off-main native loading. ASR stays on the selected local/BYOK route. Model/queue failures keep original recording active and show stop manually; no silent RMS substitution occurs.</p><p>New settings preserve the user’s RMS interval but encode legacy auto-stop as zero while neural mode is enabled. Preparation, timer events and late cleanup use per-session leases, and the original app/field/passage is checked again before microphone startup. The exact source passes {ui["checks"]["swift_tests"]} Swift / {ui["checks"]["python_tests"]} Python tests and 17 real profile CLI cases in macOS CI, plus native app/report build and clean-runner bundled imports.</p><p>A real corrupt-cache test found that Hub SDK {esc(prepared["versions"]["huggingface-hub"])} force-download could still return a bad snapshot. Repair now uses fresh local staging, checks every known file, installs a unique OSpr-owned version and atomically publishes its locator. Shared snapshots/immutable blobs and prior reader versions stay untouched. The frozen reproduction passes empty-cache preparation, one-byte same-size corruption rejection, explicit repair, native verification and {prepared["probes"]["successful_partial_probes"]:,} actual Core ML CPU probes from the relocated model. SDK transfer caches may be reused; network bytes are not measured.</p><p>Native Settings acceptance is narrower: an isolated QA app successfully enabled the toggle, selected three seconds and displayed Preferences saved. Persisted settings contain neural=true, silence=3, legacy auto-stop=0 and the prior RMS interval=3. Normal OSpr stayed running with unchanged settings/history. QA had disabled services, auto-paste/history off, and zero audio/history/recovery records.</p><p class="small muted">macOS locked before native Models download/refresh and restart could be checked. Only QA was stopped for cleanup; this is not a graceful-quit, microphone, physical shortcut, insertion or device acceptance result. A final-source QA candidate is staged with a disposable empty model cache and has not been relaunched while locked. No new downloadable ZIP is claimed. At this frozen source, final ASR edges and the delivered preview retain RMS behavior; this milestone changes automatic microphone finish only. Newer final-edge work is tracked in Progress. Pauses can end a take and the policy does not infer semantic intent. <a href="architecture/neural-endpointing.md">Contracts and remaining gates</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-ui-source-validation.json">Bound source checks</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-ui-model-preparation.json">Real preparation/repair/CPU probes</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-ui-native-settings.json">Native Settings boundary</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-ui-ci.json">CI</a>.</p></details>'''
