    panel = f'''<details id="neural-final-edges"><summary>Final-ASR neural edges: exact samples, six engines and mixed quality.</summary><p>Frozen source {esc(edges["git_commit"][:7])} adds a separate, off-by-default neural edge option shared by the app and CLI. It normalizes the complete audio once, scans those exact float32 samples with the pinned local CPU detector, checks the full PCM hash again in the worker and recognizes one outer range without a second RMS trim. Interior pauses and original timestamps stay intact. Metal still runs your selected ASR. Cloud uploads are unchanged.</p><p>All {edges["routes"]:,} routes complete: {edges["actual_asr"]:,} actual recognitions and {edges["edge_abstentions"]} detector abstentions. All {edges["exact_range_and_hash_checks"]} native ranges and hashes match references. There are zero new empty transcripts across 618 speech/model pairs. The 110 inputs reuse 104 prior cases from 33 English speakers with fixed gain/noise transforms and five synthetic negatives; six additional stereo transports repeat one speaker and a tone at 44.1/48 kHz. They are known fixtures, not 110 independent or newly held-out utterances.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>ASR</th><th>Original WER</th><th>−40 dB WER</th><th>10 dB noise WER</th><th>Better / equal / worse</th><th>New empty</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(rows)}</tbody></table></div><p>WER cells compare complete audio → neural edges on the 33-case original/quiet/noisy groups. Change counts cover 103 speech inputs per model, including four transport repetitions. Every engine has per-utterance regressions; Qwen’s noisy group worsens while Nemotron’s attenuated group improves. Raw hypotheses retain those losses. Unfiltered Whisper Turbo returns text on all five base negatives, Whisper Small on one and Qwen on three; neural edges abstain on all five for every engine. The 42 abstentions include repetitions across models/formats, not 42 distinct negative conditions.</p><p>A detector miss keeps completed recovery available. Retry without edge trimming uses the whole take for one attempt, preserves preferences and avoids stale-target insertion. Neural edges force a separate final decode rather than accepting cached streaming text; previews stay provisional. Hash/model/normalization errors stop that attempt and clean private temporary audio. Compatibility encoding prevents an older build from silently replacing neural edges with RMS.</p><p class="small muted">Source checks and macOS CI pass {source["checks"]["swift_tests"]} Swift / {source["checks"]["python_tests"]} Python tests and 17 profile CLI cases, plus app/report build and clean-runner imports. The independent checker rehashes 110 waveforms, all manifests and score totals; six transport controls preserve earlier-CLI raw probabilities. Native edge controls, recovery retry, preview-to-final interaction, microphone/shortcuts, devices and insertion remain open while macOS is locked. Defaults and the previously delivered preview are unchanged. Synthetic attenuation is not real whispering; these read-English cases do not establish multilingual/spontaneous quality. Fixed full-then-edge ordering and decoder timers do not measure end-to-end or comparative latency, energy or a product ranking. <a href="architecture/neural-endpointing.md">Implementation and acceptance gates</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-final-edges.json">Results and regressions</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-final-edges.traces.json.gz">Every hypothesis and manifest</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-final-edges-checks.json">Stored-evidence checks</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-final-edges-transport-control.json.gz">Earlier-CLI transport scores</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-final-edges-source-validation.json">Source checks</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-final-edges-ci.json">CI</a>.</p></details>'''
