    panel = f'''<details id="multilingual-neural-edges"><summary>Multilingual follow-up: 32 new empty outputs and quiet-speech deletions.</summary><p>The English study’s zero new empty result does not generalize. Frozen harness {esc(study["git_commit"][:7])} uses the delivered source {esc(study["build"]["git_commit"][:7])} CLI on all fifty existing FLEURS clips at original gain and fixed −40 dB. Documented coverage excludes Parakeet Hindi/Japanese/Mandarin and Cohere Hindi before looking at outputs. All {study["routes"]:,} routes complete: {study["actual_asr"]:,} recognitions and {study["abstentions"]} detector abstentions across 520 supported model/input pairs. The checker verifies every normalized waveform, full PCM hash and native range against an earlier raw-score control.</p><p>There are <strong>32 new empty transcripts</strong>, including two nonempty detector ranges whose recognition becomes empty. Partial deletions remain as well: quiet German Parakeet WER rises 4.10% → 22.13%, and quiet Mandarin Qwen CER rises 5.99% → 30.52%. These are detector/policy and recognition-quality failures, despite correct range transfer. Keep neural edges off for quiet/multilingual use while selection work continues. A nonempty partial result can lose content; recovery retention currently protects an empty result.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Engine</th><th>Language</th><th>Metric</th><th>Original full → edge</th><th>−40 dB full → edge</th><th>New empty / 20</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(rows)}</tbody></table></div><p>Each metric cell uses ten known source clips; the attenuated variants repeat them. Japanese/Mandarin CER strips whitespace with the same punctuation normalization; Spanish/German/Hindi use WER. Aggregate improvement on one group does not establish reliable transcription, and every hypothesis/regression remains published. No new negative controls, held-out spontaneous dictation or actual whispering are tested here.</p><p class="small muted">The same stored-evidence checker finds {len(checked["timing_issues"])} Whisper intervals beyond the analyzed range, six beyond the complete source. One 0.8-second selection gets a 29.98-second interval. This is separate from the detector-quality failure and is addressed by the newer source guard below. The signed preview still contains the old behavior; both neural options remain off by default. Native microphone/shortcuts/insertion and warning/export acceptance remain open. <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-edges-multilingual-v1.json">All group metrics and regressions</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-edges-multilingual-v1.traces.json.gz">Every reference, hypothesis and control score</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/neural-edges-multilingual-v1-checks.json">Independent checks and timing failures</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/fixtures/neural-edges-multilingual-protocol.json">Frozen selection and language coverage sources</a>.</p></details>'''
