    panel = f'''<details id="native-timing-acceptance"><summary>Later native check: timing warning and JSON/SRT export verified; normal app restored.</summary><p>The isolated checked source 9a51603 imports the public quiet Japanese 005 fixture through the native picker using Whisper Small/ja with both edge filters off. Studio and History show the timing-bound warning. Native save panels produce SRT ending at <strong>00:00:06,960</strong> and JSON with duration/segment end 6.96 and the warning. Both files are owner-only. The UI rounds duration to 7.0 s; the structured/timed exports retain the exact bound.</p><figure><img alt="Native History showing the warning and public Japanese transcription" src="data:image/png;base64,{proof}" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:12px" loading="lazy"><figcaption class="small muted">Actual isolated native app. Public-source speech only; this verifies warning presentation, not transcription correctness.</figcaption></figure><p class="small muted">A separate countdown starts real capture but reports ChatGPT rather than the intended TextEdit destination. It is discarded before ASR or public fixture playback; insertion is still unverified. The generated TextEdit space is removed/saved through UI. QA and its worker stop with zero recovery files, and the normal older app is visibly restored with eight sessions/265 words and unchanged settings/history hashes. Seeking, native VTT, physical Fn/PTT, device and successful insertion gates remain. <a href="../benchmarks/results/full-audio-native-timing.json">Exact native and cleanup boundary</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/native-timing-ja005.json">Native JSON export</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/native-timing-ja005.srt">Native SRT export</a> · <a href="assets/timing-warning-history.png">Screenshot</a>.</p></details>'''
