    panel = f'''<details id="preview-cadence"><summary>Preview cadence source change: steady deadlines, mixed first-partial results.</summary><p>The old loop slept after each decode, so nominal 320 ms feeds included the processing time again. New monotonic deadlines retain one request in flight, admit one update after an overrun and fence stale generations before snapshot. Missing session IDs no longer fall through to offline packet transcription. A preview failure becomes visible while recording and final fallback remain available. Local checks pass 310 Swift / 178 Python tests, five scheduler tests, lint and release app/CLI builds.</p><p>The actual Core probe supplies fixed-cost request schedules. Six real Nemotron sessions receive the same 960,000-sample 16 kHz waveform: ten complete public Quilter utterances in sixty seconds. Every submitted PCM hash and final text matches; WER is zero on this repeated fixture. Independent schedule/metric checks pass. <strong>First partial is not uniformly earlier</strong>, and request counts increase.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Modeled work</th><th>Live requests: old → deadline</th><th>First partial modeled delivery</th><th>Final transcript</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(rows)}</tbody></table></div><p><strong>Native-rate continuity remains a separate defect.</strong> The fifteen-case stateless normalization diagnostic matches all five 16 kHz controls; all ten 44.1/48 kHz cases differ from full-file PCM. One second in 1,024-frame packets yields 16,021 / 16,031 samples instead of 16,000. Even equal counts can hide changed filter boundaries. Capture snapshots use native input rate, so bounded continuous resampling and final-tail verification are the next streaming requirement. This scheduling change does not solve that gap.</p><p class="small muted">No wall-clock pacing, microphone/UI latency or energy measurements. Work costs are synthetic and requests complete in the replay rather than being canceled at user stop. A repeated speaker is not general accuracy evidence. More frequent work can cost more GPU/energy; preview remains opt-in. Native cadence/failure/stop/device acceptance is open. The checked 9a51603 preview ZIP predates this source change. <a href="../benchmarks/results/preview-cadence-real.json">Core schedules and paired results</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/preview-cadence-real.traces.json.gz">Every real partial and transcript</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/preview-cadence-checks.json">Independent checks and regressions</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/preview-native-packet-normalization.json">Native-rate defect cases</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/preview-cadence-source-validation.json">Bound source checks</a> · <a href="architecture/preview-cadence.md">Behavior and remaining acceptance</a>.</p></details>'''
