if native_stop_path.is_file():
    study = json.loads(native_stop_path.read_text())
    panel = f'''<details id="native-stream-stop"><summary>Native IPC stop replay: canceled packets survive, replacement and fallback controls match.</summary><p>A standalone benchmark compiles the unchanged shipping Swift WorkerClient and uses its real owned Python worker with cached Metal Nemotron. Ten scenarios at 44.1/48 kHz exercise normal feed/tail/flush, an already-canceled caller, cancellation while awaiting a response, replacement followed by a stale session cancel, and complete-file fallback after a rate-change error and worker restart. <strong>All ten final text controls match.</strong></p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Boundary</th><th>Observed result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Already canceled before request</td><td>{study["already_cancelled_requests_preserved"]}/2 admitted packets preserved, no restart</td></tr><tr><td>Cancel between request start and return</td><td>{study["timed_cancellations_between_request_and_return"]}/2 timer orderings observed; final text matches</td></tr><tr><td>Stale UUID cancel after replacement</td><td>{study["stale_cancel_rejections"]}/2 rejected without clearing the new session</td></tr><tr><td>Rate-change error → restart → full-file fallback</td><td>{study["restarted_worker_fallbacks"]}/2 text controls match</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The six stop-path transcripts and both fallback transcripts have zero WER on one known public 12.485-second English source. Both replacement transcripts match their fresh controls but retain <strong>5.88% WER</strong>: conservative scoring counts “Mr.” versus “MISTER” as one error in seventeen words. The scoring normalization is unchanged. The first twelve-second packet takes roughly 184–241 ms across caller intervals; these diagnostic, unpaced request times are not native dictation latency.</p><p class="small muted">The independent checker verifies frozen sources, native PCM recipes/counts, caller ordering, PID relationships, text controls and edit distances. Temporary WAVs are decoded and byte-checked by the producer; ephemeral file hashes are bookkeeping. No assertion that a GPU kernel was executing at the cancellation instant, and retaining admitted input is intentional. This does not operate microphone capture, Capture.snapshot, AppModel.stop, UI, insertion or physical Fn/PTT. All owned replay workers exit. Later native cleanup quits QA and restores normal OSpr with unchanged settings/history. No production model, default or ZIP change. <a href="../benchmarks/results/native-stream-stop.json">Native receipt and source pins</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/native-stream-stop.traces.json.gz">Every response, transcript and timing</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/native-stream-stop-checks.json">Independent checks</a> · <a href="architecture/native-stream-stop.md">Behavior and remaining native gates</a>.</p></details>'''
