    panel = f'''<details id="runtime-footprint"><summary>Runtime size study: APIs work without Torch, but one Qwen name regresses.</summary><p>A temporary package tree omits only Torch’s RECORD-owned entries; all other modules, the checked bundled interpreter and backend remain identical. Thirty smoke requests pass. A frozen broader replay completes <strong>422 API requests, including 404 file-transcription requests</strong>, with zero API errors. {study["text_pairs"] - len(study["text_differences"])}/{study["text_pairs"]} text pairs match, including all 52 multilingual and thirty nonspeech controls. Notes, diarization and streaming controls match too. <strong>The full Torch runtime remains the default.</strong></p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Known English slice</th><th>Clips</th><th>WER: full → no Torch</th><th>Word errors / reference words</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table></div><p>Qwen changes <strong>“Nelly” → “Nellie”</strong> on source 1089-134686-0004; the reference uses NELLY. Transformers selects Torch or NumPy feature extraction based on library presence, even when MLX Qwen requests NumPy tensors. A six-call same-model diagnostic reproduces the spelling twice per backend: Torch gives Nelly, NumPy and a SciPy F32 trial give Nellie. The upstream F32 feature arrays differ by at most 1.2636185e−5. Independent feature recomputation confirms their hashes and that maximum; a small numeric difference can affect a proper name.</p><p>Torch-owned entries occupy 523,975,219 regular-file bytes and contribute 124,925,792 compressed bytes inside the existing checked ZIP, excluding archive headers. <strong>No smaller distributable is built or promoted.</strong> The diagnostic also observes two identical feature extractions per request: the pinned Qwen generator repeats preprocessing for prompt-token accounting. Exact reuse is a separate optimization candidate, without replacing the current frontend.</p><p class="small muted">Known inputs, one pair, candidate first in the broader replay and baseline first in smoke. This is compatibility/regression evidence, not a significance test, general model ranking, calibrated memory/energy or latency comparison. Raw final MLX counters can include Engine’s per-request resets. The independent checker reconstructs 202 normalized PCM recipes and edit distances; ephemeral WAV headers are not reconstructed. The SciPy trial uses a Torch-generated window constant in a process with Torch installed. No model, default, dependency lock or checked-package changes. <a href="../benchmarks/results/runtime-footprint-full.json">Frozen broader replay</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/runtime-footprint-full.traces.json.gz">Every response and hypothesis</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/runtime-footprint-full-checks.json">Independent source/PCM/metric checks</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/qwen-frontend-precision.json">Same-model feature controls</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/qwen-frontend-precision-checks.json">Recomputed upstream features</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/runtime-footprint-size.json">Measured current archive entries</a> · <a href="architecture/runtime-footprint.md">Method and promotion gates</a>.</p></details>'''
