    panel = f'''<details id="qwen-prompt-accounting"><summary>Qwen duplicate-work study: exact outputs, no measured speedup.</summary><p>The pinned generator reprocesses audio after its first token solely to count prompt tokens. A smaller adapter captures the actual prompt length instead, retaining one integer and delegating encoding/sampling to the unchanged stream and Torch frontend. Unknown private source, stochastic frontends and unsupported streams retain original accounting. Hooks restore on success/error; the actual bound generator owner is used.</p><p><strong>Both trials preserve 105 exact paired payloads and all 124 native payloads.</strong> In each, 96 direct pairs reduce frontend evaluations 2→1; six zero-token pairs stay at one and three exact-zero pairs stay at zero. Every native optimized call reduces 2→1. Lower work counts alone do not establish lower latency.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Native median: baseline → trial</th><th>Native p95: baseline → trial</th><th>Predeclared gate</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table></div><p><strong>Reuse remains off by default.</strong> The gate required strictly lower native p50 and p95 within +5%. Neither trial passes: medians rise 0.098% and 0.180%. The normal path installs no hooks; explicit research setting <code>OSPR_QWEN_FEATURE_REUSE=1</code> enables prompt accounting. The checked streaming-v0 app/ZIP remains unchanged. Local validation passes 310 Swift / 248 Python tests and lint.</p><p class="small muted">Known 35-case corpus, three counterbalanced repeats; native ABBA blocks each have one cold call and thirty warm calls, using one public 5.215-second clip and automatic language. Shared-system drift is visible; absolute times across the two trials are not a candidate comparison. No significance, energy, physical microphone/UI or consumer-product ranking claim. The independent checker reconstructs PCM hashes, pair order, payload/counter checks and quantiles without rerunning recognition. Two earlier owner/AST guard failures remain as incomplete raw traces. A fresh TextEdit handoff also remains open: OSpr captured Google Chrome as target; capture was discarded before ASR/insertion and normal OSpr restored with unchanged settings/history. <a href="../benchmarks/results/qwen-prompt-accounting.json">Prompt-count receipt</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/qwen-prompt-accounting-v2.traces.json.gz">Every prompt-count response</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/qwen-prompt-accounting-checks.json">Independent checks</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/qwen-feature-cache.json">Feature-cache negative result</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/qwen-feature-reuse-active.traces.json.gz">Every cache response</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/qwen-feature-cache-checks.json">Cache checks</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/results/qwen-reuse-attempts.json">Rejected attempt index</a> · <a href="architecture/qwen-prompt-accounting.md">Method and remaining gates</a>.</p></details>'''
